<title>USA: Farm-wheel tractor sales down 8.3 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Farm-wheel tractor sales down 8.3 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Equipment Manufacturers Institute said Tuesday total farm-wheel tractor sales fell 8.3 percent in January to 6,510 units from 7,100 units in the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>Total two-wheel farm tractors declined to 6,234 units compared to 6,809 units in January 1996, the trade group reported. Four-wheel drive farm tractor sales fell 5.2 percent to 276 units from 291.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
